# Third-party notices

The text of this skill is adapted from the DeepSeek Harness UI review skills and generalised to browser-rendered UI changes in any software project.

- Upstream: <https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness>, pinned at `dsh-v0.2.2-rc.5` (`9c2670d3bce5275e0d1610272958121af87787bb`).
- Upstream paths:
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-client-ui-ux/SKILL.md` — the impact-scaled review workflow, minimum rendered checks, interaction and feedback rules, and evidence handoff.
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-client-ui-ux/references/alignment.md` — the distinction between layout boxes, targets, and painted results, and the requirement to name the aligned objects and axes.
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-client-ui-ux/references/spacing.md` — grouping by object or action, rendered-gap comparison, and reuse of project spacing.
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-client-ui-ux/references/icons.md` — consumer-local icon reuse and the distinction between control geometry and artwork.
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-responsive-ui/SKILL.md` — the supported narrow viewport, access to primary actions, text wrapping and truncation, focus preservation, input capability, and hover-versus-touch principles.
  - `.agents/skills/record-browser-gif/SKILL.md` — truthful browser evidence from the changed build, with capture and publication kept separate.
- Relation: adapted. The project-level rendered-evidence workflow, impact-scaled inspection, consumer tracing, minimum state checks, accessibility-sensitive interaction checks, before-and-after preservation, and honest scope reporting are carried. DeepSeek Harness tokens, component paths, platform clearance, product pages, designer roster, approval policy, source-specific viewport values, and mandatory GUI-PR policy are replaced by the adopting project's declared system, supported surfaces and evidence policy. The browser recording is a default evidence requirement rather than a dependency; a project may declare an equivalent form.

